## Agreed design decisions

| # | Decision |
|---|---|
| 1 | All official **published/SaaS docs** live in **`05 - InfoSec / 02 - Official Other Policies`** under a flat numbered scheme — `01. SaaS - Terms of Use`, `02. SaaS - DPA`, `11/12/13. Website - Privacy/Cookie/Terms of Use`, `21/22. Application - Privacy/Cookie`. (The SLA is a contract attachment, not a policy → deferred, not here.) Each is a folder holding its dated `- LATEST` file. _(Supersedes earlier placements: SaaS-default-agreements, Marketing, Product&Tech Published-policies — all reverted to this.)_ |
| 2 | **Marketplace (privacy-first) and SaaS (experimentation-first) are separate lineages** — kept apart even while currently identical. |
| 3 | **Version unit = the whole contract package**, snapshotted together. A snapshot is cut when the **offer/agreements change materially** — not per customer, not per minor edit. To change: copy the latest snapshot forward into a new dated folder and edit there. |
| 4 | Templates split by motion: **`01 - Microsoft Marketplace Template`** + **`02 - Customer Cloud Hosting Template`** (singular). All package content lives **inside dated snapshot subfolders**. |
| 5 | **Every document carries its own in-doc effective/version date** (DPA + SLA header; each subprocessor appendix its own "last updated"). That date **MUST equal the snapshot folder name** (`YYYY-MM-DD`). The signed copy in a customer folder is therefore self-describing — it *is* the per-customer version record; no external sheet is the source of truth. |
| 6 | **All DPA templates embed the subprocessor list as an appendix** (the embedded appendix is the customer-facing source of truth; the InfoSec standalone list is the internal working master that feeds them). Appendix structure standardized across templates; the empty appendix populated. Any template change is **dated today** and created in **`… - DRAFT`** first, promoted to `… - LATEST` on finalisation. Already-signed DPAs are not changed. |

## Snapshot naming convention

- Suffix marks status: `… - LATEST` = active · `… - DRAFT` = work in progress · (no suffix) = superseded history. ISO date sorts chronologically.
- **Container depends on content:**
  - **Packages** (multi-file, e.g. the enterprise template motions) → dated **subfolders**: `YYYY-MM-DD - LATEST/`.
  - **Single documents** (subprocessor list, SaaS policies, SaaS DPA/SLA) → dated **files**: `<Name> - YYYY-MM-DD - LATEST`. No subfolder, no separate archive folder — superseded versions are just bare-date files alongside.
- **Lifecycle:** `… - DRAFT` → finalize (rename to `… - LATEST`, drop `- LATEST` from the prior active) → superseded (drop suffix → bare date).
- **Invariant:** exactly **one** `- LATEST` per folder; zero-or-more `- DRAFT`; all others bare-date.
- The in-doc effective date (decision 5) must match the folder/filename date.
- This convention + the copy-forward / never-edit-a-used-snapshot rule lives **once** in `05 - InfoSec / 03 - Procedures & Runbooks` (extend the existing policy-update runbook) — not duplicated per folder.

